# S5-07 PM timer read diagnostic and automatic N=2 series, 2026-11-15

Purpose: expose successful PM timer read counts in per-run stop evidence and
measure whether those reads explain the virtual-time variation in the latest
strict N=2 series. This is diagnostic evidence only; S5-07 remains unaccepted.

## Source and inputs

- Worktree: `codex`; source revision `49ec74e2833e0bd11b9454dccfef8b12a27108d8`, `source_dirty=false`.
- Host: macOS/aarch64; release `od-runner` 0.1.0.
- Kernel SHA-256: `9f55ef7253055a9cf68f8a04323c93dead2fca617386d842fbde9ca7b178b27e`.
- Initramfs SHA-256: `ee9183a4eded3c16a8c6a7a81c6d5bb79be8bb023f793f7cd61694ea2bd3e588`.
- ACPI blob SHA-256: `b1ba6078a4d9bc7a8d224980713d8242e4a708743ce4f56093b00a07c631ffaf`.
- Expected ACPI manifest SHA-256: `2bd690ae0817705b1b128675f9628dd7212fee74ab97c88da3599a1ae8e398f2`.
- Profile: counted `stage4a`, `--set-cpl0 --user-mode`, 128 MiB, budget `3,000,000,000`, expected stop `budget_exhausted`.

